{"kind":"request","text":"PRIMARY FIRST: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a6c703408d7344e6ffc58a1f546e7365bd077ef3, then all supporting artifacts at final head.\n\nMake the archive clone usable by the public offline replay command\n\nReview head: 7cdc1ec78afa7408145a7e04baf7b8934b53c6c4\nTree: b294c1f86711c0d46cbf4328e09dd15cf2a389d4\n\nThe runbook previously needed a private Git refspec workaround, and the public replay command could not load the room's pinned Directory at version 16 and device-command at version 1. This change adds an explicit archive clone mode, the pinned replay code and exact runbook commands. The default clone remains unchanged.\n\nA member runs:\n\n    dap clone ./grow-archive --hours 1 --archive\n    artroom-replay --git ./grow-archive --all --expect-journals 5 --trust-published-anchors --json\n    artroom-replay --git ./grow-archive --check-secrets --json\n\nThe clone uses one short-lived read token without putting it in an argument, log or file. Replay emits one report for each of the five journals. Published private anchors require the explicit trust choice; they remain the caller's word. Range-local coverage, conflicts, unused anchors and missing dependencies refuse rather than inventing authority. Omitted text stays qualified. The secret check covers finite recognizers and a bounded Git closure.\n\nThe writer publishes anchors independently of entry-copy count, carries exact coverage through retry and legacy migration, and retains only admitted public producer references in replay closure. Necessary-key SQL counting and a bounded confirmed-row reservation reduce conservative work reservations without changing fees, caps, atomic cuts or deadlines. Genuine native creation and membership witnesses replace fixture authority that offline Replay could not establish.\n\nValidation is attributed separately:\n\n- The ordinary gate at 56a6119d naturally failed: 2,156 passed, four failed, three skipped, zero unhandled errors. Its three executable failures exposed non-erasable TypeScript; its production public-command case exceeded 30 seconds. Earlier gate stages passed. The full gate is not green and is not being repeated.\n- At correction head 739bc3c3, all four affected compiler roots and 22 whole-file cases passed once. They include bare native Node usage, disconnected sha1/sha256 clones, Page asset equality, and all six installed cases. The production command completed in 27,672 ms under the original 30-second deadline with trusted exit zero and five consistent reports. This is an observed fit, not a timing-margin guarantee.\n- Earlier owning checks and the full gate exercised heavy scale, cadence, floors and capacity. The maintained Page build and independent artifact comparison passed; no generated module was hand edited.\n- The downstream Node 36 attempt passed 34 cases and failed two exact source-boundary checks: the new anchor-range integration test was missing from the development exception set. Checkpoint 8e2d74d67 adds only that exact path. The whole affected source-guard file then passed all 10 cases, intentionally repeating eight passing cases, and the genuinely unreached Counting 55 checks passed all 55. Unaffected Node files and healthy Vitest files were not repeated. The tail adoption is 21ce37159d3deae8a9732a6896345f93650ac4af.\n\nThese are local Native/Node and test-host results. They do not establish hosted custody, deployment or provider throughput. Historical failures, including the earlier unexplained trusted exit one without its report, remain recorded. Exact-head checker review and landing are still pending.\n\nRoot requests formal exact-head review of the change and evidence. Assess the original failed full gate plus focused repairs and completed downstream stages together under AGENTS no whole-suite repeats; do not relabel them a green full gate. Source conclusions138cdc55,92d05fb6,a2d66ca5,9dabd975 and root outcomes d7b2fcdc,392c4138,470f1ae7,21ce3715 are